            <ArticleTitle>Atypical clinical presentation of internal herniation after laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-years old women with history of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass presented with progressive abdominal pain, mainly at the left loin. Imaging was aspecific. Exploratory laparoscopy showed an internal herniation trough the Petersen space.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
